{"id":"NCT05720936","title":"In-hospital Stellate Ganglion Block for Arrhythmic Storm","official":"A Multicenter Observational Study on In-hospital Stellate Ganglion Block for Arrhythmic Storm","summary":"Arrhythmic storm is a real emergency and its treatment could be challenging. Antiarrhythmic drugs are few and often ineffective. Neuromodulation has been grown in evidences but no large multicentric studies are present in literature about safety and effectiveness of Percutaneous Stellate Ganglion Block (PSGB). Patients with an electrical storm refractory to at least one antiarrhythmic drug will receive PSGB and will be enrolled in the present study.\n\nThe number of defibrillations before and after the treatment will be compared, complications will be annotated.","conditions":["Arrhythmic Storm","Electrical Storm","Ventricular Fibrillation","Ventricular Tachycardia"],"interventions":[{"type":"PROCEDURE","name":"Percutaneous stellate ganglion block (PSGB)"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* age ≥ 18 years,\n* presence of arrhythmic storm defined as more than three sustained ventricular arrhythmias in 24 hours refractory to the standard medical treatment.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* A previous history of cardiac sympathicectomy\n* Having a neck judged unsuitable for the procedure (previous neck surgery, previous burns, presence of large scars, thyroid goiter)\n\nBoth the two approaches present in literature and commonly used for this technique are allowed for the study:\n\n* The \"anatomical\" approach which consist in the identification of the Chassaignac's tubercle that represents the point of needle insertion\n* The \"echo-guided\" approach Regardless to the approach (anatomical or echo-guided) the doctor will be able to choose, according to the clinical characteristics of the patients, whether to perform a single shot injection of anesthetic or a continuous infusion of anesthetic. In the second case a catheter will be left in place and connected to an infusion pump.","minAge":"","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":500,"start":"2017-11-07","pcd":"2028-12-31","upd":"2025-06-08","sponsor":"Fondazione IRCCS Policlinico San Matteo di Pavia","areas":["other"],"central":["Simone Savastano, MD · +39 0382501590 · s.savastano@smatteo.pv.it","Alessia Currao, PharmD (CRC) · +39 0382501590 · a.currao@smatteo.pv.it"],"sites":[{"f":"A.O. SS. Antonio e Biagio e Cesare Arrigo di Alessandria.","city":"Alessandria","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":44.9092,"lon":8.6101,"c":"Edoardo Gandolfi, MD · edogand@hotmail.com"},{"f":"Ospedale di Bentivoglio","city":"Bentivoglio","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":44.6369,"lon":11.4174,"c":"Giulio Boggian, MD · g.boggian@ausl.bologna.it"},{"f":"Ospedale Maggiore di Bologna","city":"Bologna","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":44.4938,"lon":11.3387,"c":"Ganmarco Iannopollo, MD · gianmarco.iannopollo@libero.it"},{"f":"Cardiology Department, Fondazione IRCCS Policlinico San Matteo","city":"Pavia","pr":"","zip":"27100","s":"R","lat":45.1921,"lon":9.1592,"c":"Simone Savastano, MD · +39 0382501590 · s.savastano@smatteo.pv.it"},{"f":"Ospedale Civile","city":"Voghera","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":44.9915,"lon":9.0117,"c":"Sara Compagnoni, MD · sara_compagnoni@asst-pavia.it"},{"f":"Ospedale Mater Salutis","city":"Legnago","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":45.1936,"lon":11.3023,"c":"Antonio Mugnolo, MD · antonio.mugnolo@aulss9.veneto.it"},{"f":"A.O.U. delle Marche, Ospedali Riuniti","city":"Ancona","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":43.6072,"lon":13.5103,"c":"Matilda Shkoza, MD · matilda.shkoza@ospedaliriuniti.marche.it"},{"f":"Ospedale Cardinal Massaia","city":"Asti","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":44.9016,"lon":8.2075,"c":"Marco Scaglione, MD · marco.scaglione.at@gmail.com"},{"f":"Policlinico S. Orsola-Malpighi, IRCCS A.O.U. Bologna","city":"Bologna","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":44.4938,"lon":11.3387,"c":"Matteo Ziacchi, MD · matteo.ziacchi@aosp.bo.it"},{"f":"P.O. \